      "hints": [
        "Write $\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta} - \\tan\\theta = \\frac{1 - \\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$.",
        "Square and replace $\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta = (1 - \\sin\\theta)(1 + \\sin\\theta)$.",
        "Cancel $(1 - \\sin\\theta)$ to obtain $\\frac{1 - \\sin\\theta}{1 + \\sin\\theta}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express the terms inside the parentheses in terms of $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta} - \\tan\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta} - \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} = \\frac{1 - \\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$$",
        "Square the quotient and apply the identity $\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta$:\n$$\\left(\\frac{1 - \\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\right)^2 = \\frac{(1 - \\sin\\theta)^2}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{(1 - \\sin\\theta)^2}{1 - \\sin^2\\theta}$$",
        "Factorise the difference of two squares in the denominator and cancel the common factor $(1 - \\sin\\theta)$:\n$$\\frac{(1 - \\sin\\theta)^2}{(1 - \\sin\\theta)(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{1 - \\sin\\theta}{1 + \\sin\\theta} = \\text{RHS}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Trigonometric Proof": "Combines fractions to $\\frac{1-\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ (M1). Squares and uses $1-\\sin^2\\theta$ (M1). Cancels factor to show RHS (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
